1
00:00:02,660 --> 00:00:05,220
Hyper Elementary Schoolers vs. Duos

2
00:00:31,320 --> 00:00:32,440
D-don't just stand there looking troubled!

3
00:00:32,660 --> 00:00:33,600
What are you doing!

4
00:00:34,100 --> 00:00:35,840
Hey! It's over now, you know!

5
00:00:36,360 --> 00:00:37,080
What is it!

6
00:00:37,340 --> 00:00:39,000
Could I borrow the map, please?

7
00:00:39,340 --> 00:00:40,920
Here, go find it yourself.

8
00:00:42,100 --> 00:00:43,800
What year is this map edition from?

9
00:00:44,360 --> 00:00:45,380
How would I know that!

10
00:00:46,160 --> 00:00:48,080
It's the latest edition,
published this year.

11
00:00:49,180 --> 00:00:49,780
Thanks.

12
00:00:50,080 --> 00:00:50,800
No, not at all.

13
00:00:51,140 --> 00:00:53,880
Officer Nakagawa, back from patrol.

14
00:00:54,220 --> 00:00:54,980
Thank you for your hard work.

15
00:00:55,680 --> 00:00:56,360
I see.

16
00:00:57,100 --> 00:00:59,840
So this river was filled
in and turned into a road.

17
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:01,460
That's right.

18
00:01:02,360 --> 00:01:04,740
Alright, let's convert the Navicon software.

19
00:01:05,560 --> 00:01:06,500
Navicon?

20
00:01:07,360 --> 00:01:08,600
You've got one of those?

21
00:01:09,080 --> 00:01:09,400
Yeah.

22
00:01:09,940 --> 00:01:11,680
Could I borrow your desk for a moment?

23
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:12,520
Sure.

24
00:01:18,600 --> 00:01:20,700
So it has a PC built into it?

25
00:01:21,820 --> 00:01:23,400
Where's the keyboard?

26
00:01:24,660 --> 00:01:25,440
An abacus?

27
00:01:25,440 --> 00:01:27,420
Looks like it's not just a regular abacus.

28
00:01:28,780 --> 00:01:29,420
I see.

29
00:01:35,300 --> 00:01:36,680
What amazing finger work!

30
00:01:43,800 --> 00:01:46,100
Is this some cheap junk keyboard?

31
00:01:49,100 --> 00:01:50,440
Change complete.

32
00:01:50,940 --> 00:01:52,900
Wow, that's amazing, that's amazing!

33
00:01:53,480 --> 00:01:54,440
I'll save it.

34
00:01:54,440 --> 00:01:56,020
That's quite something, isn't it.

35
00:01:56,020 --> 00:01:58,560
It's one o'clock, time for cram school.

36
00:01:59,160 --> 00:02:01,560
It even manages your schedule? Impressive.

37
00:02:02,360 --> 00:02:04,100
Oh no, I'm going to miss cram school!

38
00:02:04,100 --> 00:02:06,440
