on getting him to take the checkup.

148
00:07:22,300 --> 00:07:23,900
You don't have to go that far.

149
00:07:26,040 --> 00:07:29,020
It's impossible. He's like a loose cannon.

150
00:07:30,160 --> 00:07:33,940
Isn't there some way to find him?
At this rate, my neck is...

151
00:07:34,860 --> 00:07:36,800
That's it! Let's call Plus-kun.

152
00:07:41,360 --> 00:07:43,080
Come on, step right up, step right up!

153
00:07:43,240 --> 00:07:46,520
Now you can watch movies that are
just out in theaters right at home!

154
00:07:47,360 --> 00:07:49,140
And it's only 1,000 yen per tape.

155
00:07:49,300 --> 00:07:50,500
Come on, buy, buy!

156
00:07:50,820 --> 00:07:51,600
Just one tape.

157
00:07:51,860 --> 00:07:52,340
Interesting.

158
00:07:53,940 --> 00:07:54,800
About eight tapes.

159
00:07:56,880 --> 00:07:58,910
This is a money-maker.

160
00:07:58,960 --> 00:08:01,300
Nah, it's all good.

161
00:08:01,880 --> 00:08:04,820
Phone call. Could it be the
president of Super Denshi Kogi?

162
00:08:05,760 --> 00:08:06,320
Hello?

163
00:08:07,160 --> 00:08:09,580
Hey, Ryotsu!

164
00:08:11,360 --> 00:08:11,840
Don't you dare take a day off!

165
00:08:12,780 --> 00:08:15,380
Chief! How do you know this number?

166
00:08:16,340 --> 00:08:18,120
I know everything about you.

167
00:08:18,460 --> 00:08:21,140
Ryotsu, get your health checkup today!

168
00:08:21,600 --> 00:08:23,040
Get back here right now!

169
00:08:23,620 --> 00:08:24,860
Ugh, you're so annoying.

170
00:08:28,180 --> 00:08:29,480
He hung up on me!

171
00:08:30,080 --> 00:08:33,680
Nakagawa-kun,
is there no other way to track him down?

172
00:08:34,120 --> 00:08:37,780
Didn't you say you put a
transmitter on the Chief?

173
00:08:38,180 --> 00:08:40,700
I think we can trace it
back from the frequency.

174
00:08:41,320 --> 00:08:42,940
Right, let's find the transmitter.

175
00:08:42,940 --> 00:08:45,480
It should be somewhere on the Chief's body.

176
00:08:45,480 --> 00:08:48,440
Geez, when did he even...? Okay.

177
00:08:48,440 --> 00:08:52,180
Where is it, where is it, where is it?
Not here, not here, not here.

178
00:08:54,260 --> 00:08:56,580
Whoa, sorry, sorry.

179
00:08:56,580 --> 00:08:57,540
No, no.

180
00:08:58,460 --> 00:09:01,220
Is there no other way to make money

181
00:09:01,220 --> 00:09:02,280
You're fired!

182
00:09:02,280 --> 00:09:04,440
Chief, I'm sorry.

183
00:09:04,440 --> 00:09:06,340
What do you think you're doing?

184
00:09:07,780 --> 00:09:08,460
Isn't it me?

185
00:09:08,460 --> 00:09:10,860
Hundreds of millions in
profits will go down the drain!

186
00:09:11,520 --> 00:09:12,320
Hundreds of millions?

187
00:09:13,520 --> 00:09:14,700
Hey, what happened?

188
00:09:14,700 --> 00:09:17,540
The computer built into the car broke down,

189
00:09:18,100 --> 00:09:21,340
and we can't get important
information anymore.

190
00:09:22,020 --> 00:09:23,320
If it's PC communication,

191
00:09:23,320 --> 00:09:26,560
my Super Denshi GX767 can do it!

192
00:09:26,560 --> 00:09:27,620
Really?

193
00:09:27,620 --> 00:09:28,240
Yeah.

194
00:09:32,820 --> 00:09:33,620
However,

195
00:09:33,620 --> 00:09:36,000
my access fee is steep, you know.

196
00:09:37,780 --> 00:09:40,460
Looks like it,
so I'll take 10% of the profits.

197
00:09:41,160 --> 00:09:43,180
That's way too high. It's 1%.

198
00:09:43,580 --> 00:09:46,420
Fine. Let's meet in the middle.
How about 7%?

199
00:09:46,900 --> 00:09:47,840
Where's the middle?

200
00:09:48,880 --> 00:09:49,800
If you don't like it, that's fine.

201
00:09:50,460 --> 00:09:53,520
OK, OK. Let's shake on 7%.

202
00:09:54,140 --> 00:09:55,480
Alright, it's a deal. Just kidding.

203
00:09:56,760 --> 00:09:58,540
Hurry up. It's the White House.

204
00:09:58,920 --> 00:10:00,680
At exactly 5 p.m. Japan time,

205
00:10:00,700 --> 00:10:03,640
next year's orange safeguard
buyout price will be announced.

206
00:10:03,720 --> 00:10:04,560
I want to know that.

207
00:10:05,340 --> 00:10:06,220
We're running out of time, you know.

208
00:10:06,220 --> 00:10:07,560
Where's the address?

209
00:10:08,020 --> 00:10:08,500
Here it is.

210
00:10:08,500 --> 00:10:09,880
What's the password?

211
00:10:10,840 --> 00:10:11,360
Alright, then.

212
00:10:14,840 --> 00:10:15,920
That was quick.

213
00:10:15,920 --> 00:10:18,320
That's because it uses a
dedicated communications satellite.

214
00:10:19,380 --> 00:10:20,980
The orange tank has come up.

215
00:10:21,300 --> 00:10:22,340
It's higher than last year.

216
00:10:23,400 --> 00:10:26,860
Hey, contact headquarters and buy up
orange-related stocks all over the world.

217
00:10:26,860 --> 00:10:27,320
Yes.

218
00:10:31,820 --> 00:10:33,500
Sorry, my battery's dead.

219
00:10:35,040 --> 00:10:38,740
Use my phone. It's a dedicated line,
so you'll get through right away.

220
00:10:38,740 --> 00:10:40,160
Thanks!

221
00:10:42,360 --> 00:10:43,000
Found it!

222
00:10:43,640 --> 00:10:45,700
That guy's the reason our bonuses got cut.

223
00:10:46,300 --> 00:10:48,300
Give it here. I'll connect it right away.

224
00:10:49,120 --> 00:10:53,800
Ryotsu, I'll find him for sure
and make him get a health checkup.

225
00:10:56,400 --> 00:11:01,040
Wow, the Singapore mayor's orange-related
company's stock just doubled!

226
00:11:01,880 --> 00:11:03,780
Good, good, Mr. Ryotsu!

227
00:11:04,560 --> 00:11:07,200
The London stock market
should be opening soon.

228
00:11:07,200 --> 00:11:08,820
Access it!

229
00:11:08,820 --> 00:11:09,700
Got it.

230
00:11:10,400 --> 00:11:11,280
There it is! There it is!

231
00:11:11,280 --> 00:11:13,100
Where are the orange stocks?

232
00:11:13,100 --> 00:11:15,780
Trading's about to start.
London's at double!

233
00:11:16,380 --> 00:11:17,360
Good, sell it all off!

234
00:11:17,360 --> 00:11:19,980
You idiot, how can you bet on just double?

235
00:11:20,700 --> 00:11:23,320
Stocks are stocks,
but this isn't oicho-kabu, you know.

236
00:11:23,820 --> 00:11:24,660
It's pretty much the same thing.

237
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:27,200
Wait, wait, hold out until it hits triple!

238
00:11:27,660 --> 00:11:29,240
There's no way it'll go that high.

239
00:11:34,560 --> 00:11:37,060
Nice, but it's awfully rigid, isn't it.

240
00:11:37,420 --> 00:11:40,360
Thanks to you, I made about 300 million.
Thank you.

241
00:11:40,820 --> 00:11:42,920
300 million yen That's great.

242
00:11:43,220 --> 00:11:45,040
No, no, it's 300 million dollars.

243
00:11:45,240 --> 00:11:48,584
Dollars? If it's 110 yen to the dollar,

244
00:11:48,634 --> 00:11:50,520
33 billion yen?

245
00:11:50,880 --> 00:11:52,243
Yes. Now then,

246
00:11:52,293 --> 00:11:55,120
here's your cut. It was 7%, right?

247
00:11:55,660 --> 00:11:57,932
One, ten, hun...

248
00:11:57,982 --> 00:12:01,080
2.31 billion yen?

249
00:12:02,920 --> 00:12:05,160
2.31 billion yen

250
00:12:06,460 --> 00:12:08,180
Is it really all right
for me to get this much?

251
00:12:08,180 --> 00:12:10,780
Yes, a promise is a promise.

252
00:12:10,780 --> 00:12:13,600
Besides,
you have a real talent for business.

253
00:12:13,600 --> 00:12:16,340
Won't you become my partner?

254
00:12:16,340 --> 00:12:17,740
Partner?

255
00:12:18,360 --> 00:12:21,200
Become my co-owner with an
annual salary of 1 billion yen.

256
00:12:21,920 --> 00:12:23,140
1 billion yen?

257
00:12:24,400 --> 00:12:25,200
Well, you know...

258
00:12:25,200 --> 00:12:26,680
No, no, no, no!

259
00:12:26,680 --> 00:12:28,380
Okay, okay.

260
00:12:44,300 --> 00:12:45,640
Good morning.

261
00:13:01,220 --> 00:13:03,900
How does the vice president's chair feel?

262
00:13:03,900 --> 00:13:05,300
Not bad.

263
00:13:06,420 --> 00:13:07,240
Something terrible has happened!

264
00:13:07,240 --> 00:13:09,260
A cold wave has struck Ukraine,

265
00:13:09,260 --> 00:13:11,440
and the wheat has
apparently been devastated.

266
00:13:11,440 --> 00:13:12,020
What?

267
00:13:14,680 --> 00:13:17,160
The American wheat market is surging.

268
00:13:18,140 --> 00:13:21,740
Has the American wheat already
been snapped up by other investors?

269
00:13:22,540 --> 00:13:24,880
Alright, let's buy up the Australian wheat.

270
00:13:24,880 --> 00:13:26,640
Phone calls won't cut it.

271
00:13:26,640 --> 00:13:31,820
In situations like this, the best thing is to take cash
and negotiate directly with the farm owners face-to-face.

272
00:13:32,680 --> 00:13:33,000
I see.

273
00:13:34,160 --> 00:13:38,040
Vice President,
will you fly to Australia with me?

274
00:13:38,040 --> 00:13:39,560
Of course.

275
00:13:40,260 --> 00:13:42,180
I've had a direct flight waiting at Haneda.

276
00:13:42,180 --> 00:13:44,060
We'll go straight there with this.

277
00:13:44,060 --> 00:13:46,220
Just as expected of an executive.
You're different.

278
00:13:50,020 --> 00:13:52,440
Ryotsu seems to be
heading for Haneda Airport.

279
00:13:52,780 --> 00:13:55,400
Ryotsu's planning to skip town somewhere

280
00:13:56,640 --> 00:13:57,320
Kyushu?

281
00:13:57,320 --> 00:13:58,140
I wonder.

282
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:03,100
That plane there.

283
00:14:04,960 --> 00:14:05,900
Overseas, then?

284
00:14:14,860 --> 00:14:17,140
Chief, what are we going to do?

285
00:14:17,300 --> 00:14:19,220
My neck is on the line here.

286
00:14:19,220 --> 00:14:22,120
No matter what,
I'll make him get that health checkup.

287
00:14:22,600 --> 00:14:24,540
You're not getting away, Ryotsu!

288
00:14:24,540 --> 00:14:28,060
Chief, leave the plane arrangements to me.

289
00:14:32,140 --> 00:14:34,960
With this SR-71, we'll definitely catch up.

290
00:14:51,540 --> 00:14:53,000
He's tougher than I thought.

291
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:54,260
That sly old badger.

292
00:14:55,140 --> 00:14:56,500
What a busy time to call!

293
00:14:57,720 --> 00:14:58,480
Hello?

294
00:14:58,480 --> 00:14:59,460
Ryotsu!

295
00:14:59,460 --> 00:15:02,420
What are you doing,
coming all the way to Australia?

296
00:15:02,420 --> 00:15:04,340
Chief, how did you find this place?

297
00:15:04,960 --> 00:15:08,700
Uncle, I never asked you to come
overseas to keep an eye on me.

298
00:15:09,740 --> 00:15:10,560
What's wrong?

299
00:15:11,020 --> 00:15:12,000
N-nothing at all.

300
00:15:12,280 --> 00:15:14,920
Geez, and I'm in the middle
of an important business deal.

301
00:15:23,400 --> 00:15:24,240
Gyōsu!

302
00:15:25,100 --> 00:15:26,380
Come out!

303
00:15:26,660 --> 00:15:29,280
Go back to Japan right now
and get your health checkup!

304
00:15:31,560 --> 00:15:33,380
Chief, what on earth is that?

305
00:15:34,960 --> 00:15:37,506
That lunatic! I'm not getting caught here,

306
00:15:37,556 --> 00:15:39,060
Let's wrap up the deal quickly!

307
00:15:39,600 --> 00:15:41,280
Ugh! Stop, thief!

308
00:15:43,640 --> 00:15:47,800
What a splendid decision!

309
00:15:48,320 --> 00:15:49,180
Ah

310
00:15:49,320 --> 00:15:52,700
Ugh! Can't this thing go any faster? Hey!

311
00:15:53,060 --> 00:15:54,120
I can't go any faster than this!

312
00:15:54,240 --> 00:15:56,900
Ugh! Use willpower! Push it! Willpower!

313
00:15:57,400 --> 00:16:00,880
Ryotsu!
No matter where you run, you can't escape!

314
00:16:01,360 --> 00:16:03,920
I've got the Super Randoseru here, so there!

315
00:16:04,960 --> 00:16:08,440
I've got the Super Attack Case too!

316
00:16:09,080 --> 00:16:10,420
Magia Case

317
00:16:10,420 --> 00:16:13,900
Stop talking nonsense and come
back with me to get your checkup.

318
00:16:14,380 --> 00:16:16,580
I quit being a police officer,

319
00:16:16,580 --> 00:16:19,460
and became vice president with
a 1 billion yen annual salary.

320
00:16:20,300 --> 00:16:23,580
There's no way I'm getting
a police checkup now.

321
00:16:23,580 --> 00:16:26,300
What on earth are you talking about?

322
00:16:26,740 --> 00:16:30,100
I'm in a completely different
world from a mere chief like you now.

323
00:16:30,540 --> 00:16:31,420
Goodbye!

324
00:16:34,960 --> 00:16:38,660
What goodbye!
Nakagawa, can't you make a warning strike?

325
00:16:38,940 --> 00:16:40,600
I'm not armed with anything!

326
00:16:40,880 --> 00:16:42,380
Plus-kun, got anything?

327
00:16:42,500 --> 00:16:44,580
There's a flare attached to the backpack.

328
00:16:44,920 --> 00:16:45,780
I see.

329
00:16:46,200 --> 00:16:47,580
It has that kind of thing too?

330
00:16:47,880 --> 00:16:48,860
Be careful.

331
00:16:49,280 --> 00:16:50,760
Alright, that's enough.

332
00:16:53,220 --> 00:16:55,060
Ugh, you're so persistent!

333
00:16:55,380 --> 00:16:56,400
Good job, Plus-kun.

334
00:16:57,660 --> 00:16:59,020
W-what do you think you're doing!

335
00:16:59,360 --> 00:17:00,280
Here I go!

336
00:17:05,380 --> 00:17:06,660
W-what's going on?

337
00:17:06,660 --> 00:17:08,700
Damn, which one of us is
really serious about this?

338
00:17:08,700 --> 00:17:10,640
There's a missile on the backpack!

339
00:17:10,640 --> 00:17:13,300
It should have weapons for taking them down.

340
00:17:13,300 --> 00:17:14,460
Found it, found it!

341
00:17:15,160 --> 00:17:16,300
Alright!

342
00:17:21,520 --> 00:17:25,420
Alright!

343
00:17:25,420 --> 00:17:26,080
Ouch, hot!

344
00:17:26,180 --> 00:17:27,300
Aah!

345
00:17:28,440 --> 00:17:30,500
Hahaha! You dug your own grave!

346
00:17:30,780 --> 00:17:33,460
Nakagawa, deport him straight back to Japan!

347
00:17:33,520 --> 00:17:34,000
Understood!

348
00:17:38,040 --> 00:17:38,840
Right!

349
00:17:39,920 --> 00:17:40,800
Aah!

350
00:17:43,140 --> 00:17:44,600
What's this button?

351
00:17:46,620 --> 00:17:47,060
Whoa!

352
00:17:48,640 --> 00:17:49,520
Whoa!

353
00:17:50,920 --> 00:17:51,680
Yo-chan!

354
00:17:52,840 --> 00:18:05,840


355
00:18:05,840 --> 00:18:07,840
Ugh, you lucky bastard.

356
00:18:07,840 --> 00:18:08,564
Plus-kun,

357
00:18:08,614 --> 00:18:12,020
Isn't there any other
good way to catch Ryo-chan?

358
00:18:12,320 --> 00:18:15,040
I can track him, but catching him is...

359
00:18:15,480 --> 00:18:17,920
How about calling him again
and trying to persuade him?

360
00:18:18,280 --> 00:18:19,020
It's pointless.

361
00:18:20,260 --> 00:18:21,820
Wait, I've got a good idea.

362
00:18:28,240 --> 00:18:30,600
Hey, hey, this isn't a show, you know!

363
00:18:30,600 --> 00:18:30,820
Yo!

364
00:18:33,100 --> 00:18:34,300
Oi, bro!

365
00:18:34,300 --> 00:18:35,400
Here, here!

366
00:18:36,100 --> 00:18:37,300
Ryo-tsu!

367
00:18:37,300 --> 00:18:38,620
This is no time for that!

368
00:18:38,620 --> 00:18:40,520
The gold price is falling.

369
00:18:41,040 --> 00:18:43,920
Next, put all the gold our
company holds up for sale.

370
00:18:44,420 --> 00:18:45,140
Got it.

371
00:18:46,500 --> 00:18:47,560
Hurry up, Ryo-tsu!

372
00:18:47,560 --> 00:18:48,780
No need to panic.

373
00:18:49,840 --> 00:18:52,140
That's odd, I can't access it.

374
00:18:52,680 --> 00:18:53,620
What are you doing?

375
00:18:53,620 --> 00:18:56,140
If we don't hurry,
our company will suffer a huge loss!

376
00:18:56,620 --> 00:18:59,320
Even so, that's strange...

377
00:19:00,740 --> 00:19:04,220
We're losing fifty million
dollars every second!

378
00:19:04,900 --> 00:19:06,220
Hurry up, Ryotsu!

379
00:19:06,220 --> 00:19:07,480
I know, I know!

380
00:19:07,480 --> 00:19:09,800
So the fax machine was receiving something?

381
00:19:09,800 --> 00:19:11,400
No wonder we couldn't get through.

382
00:19:12,380 --> 00:19:14,740
Who's sending something at a time like this?

383
00:19:15,600 --> 00:19:16,580
It's the Chief, isn't it?

384
00:19:16,580 --> 00:19:19,580
Ryotsu, what are you doing?

385
00:19:19,980 --> 00:19:22,060
At this rate, our company is going under!

386
00:19:23,240 --> 00:19:24,900
I'll stop the fax right now, okay!

387
00:19:25,420 --> 00:19:27,280
There was no switch.

388
00:19:28,580 --> 00:19:29,260
Hey, look at that.

389
00:19:30,600 --> 00:19:31,380
The lock's engaged.

390
00:19:32,320 --> 00:19:35,300
It's already up 1.02
billion dollars, Ryotsu!

391
00:19:35,300 --> 00:19:36,940
A voice lock

392
00:19:37,720 --> 00:19:39,200
Guess we'll have to open it with a whistle.

393
00:19:39,640 --> 00:19:41,580
Wasn't it do-mi-so?

394
00:19:45,960 --> 00:19:47,200
Ryotsu.

395
00:19:47,900 --> 00:19:49,740
Or was it do-fa-la?

396
00:20:00,600 --> 00:20:02,120
No! No!

397
00:20:02,400 --> 00:20:03,040
No! No!

398
00:20:03,780 --> 00:20:04,900
Did it finally stop?

399
00:20:07,420 --> 00:20:08,580
What's with all the noise? Shut up!

400
00:20:08,720 --> 00:20:11,260
Let's see, two Chinese rice
bowls and one ramen set, right?

401
00:20:11,260 --> 00:20:12,420
Don't mess with me!

402
00:20:13,780 --> 00:20:15,220
Whoa, careful! I almost broke it.

403
00:20:16,520 --> 00:20:17,420
Dorabo!

404
00:20:17,680 --> 00:20:18,740
Dorabo!

405
00:20:19,700 --> 00:20:22,500
What are you doing?! Sell the gold, quick!

406
00:20:22,700 --> 00:20:25,840
I know! That last shot must have broken it.

407
00:20:25,840 --> 00:20:26,520
Dorabo!

408
00:20:26,640 --> 00:20:28,140
Hey, I'm the real thing!

409
00:20:28,420 --> 00:20:29,200
Dorabo!

410
00:20:30,600 --> 00:20:33,940
Ah ah, stop! Let go! It's me!
I'm Ryotsu, the owner!

411
00:20:33,940 --> 00:20:35,420
Even though it's not
the owner's fingerprint!

412
00:20:35,640 --> 00:20:37,140
I told you, I'm the owner!

413
00:20:37,640 --> 00:20:38,580
Ryotsu!

414
00:20:39,980 --> 00:20:43,140
To protect the secret data,
it will self-destruct in 60 seconds.

415
00:20:43,640 --> 00:20:44,280
What!?

416
00:20:45,480 --> 00:20:45,840
58

417
00:20:45,840 --> 00:20:47,000
Don't mess with me!

418
00:20:47,260 --> 00:20:48,420
Four!

419
00:20:48,780 --> 00:20:49,360
You bastard!

420
00:20:49,800 --> 00:20:50,980
This is no time for that!

421
00:20:51,160 --> 00:20:54,140
At this rate, the cotton will
be soaked with every 100 points!

422
00:20:54,500 --> 00:20:55,600
50 seconds left.

423
00:20:56,800 --> 00:20:58,220
Mr. Ryotsu.

424
00:20:58,640 --> 00:21:02,200
You have quite a unique sense for business.

425
00:21:02,200 --> 00:21:03,140
R-really?

426
00:21:03,540 --> 00:21:05,860
I had a feeling about that, from way back.

427
00:21:05,860 --> 00:21:09,160
And I'm not too shabby myself
for seeing it at a glance, am I?

428
00:21:10,740 --> 00:21:11,700
But...

429
00:21:11,700 --> 00:21:13,420
Hey, that's my Kogi!

430
00:21:15,280 --> 00:21:16,680
It seems my eyes are infallible!

431
00:21:16,880 --> 00:21:18,260
You're fired!

432
00:21:21,960 --> 00:21:25,260
I'll use this to cover
the losses you caused.

433
00:21:26,520 --> 00:21:26,840
3

434
00:21:27,420 --> 00:21:27,740
2

435
00:21:28,400 --> 00:21:28,720
1

436
00:21:35,540 --> 00:21:38,300
Looks like the confidential data
protection device has activated.

437
00:21:38,920 --> 00:21:39,680
Over there!

438
00:21:45,360 --> 00:21:45,578
Aaah!

439
00:21:45,628 --> 00:22:00,400
Uuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuu

440
00:22:00,400 --> 00:22:04,640
I'll do it! I'll take a checkup or anything,
just help me!

441
00:22:05,740 --> 00:22:09,640
You quit the force, didn't you?
You don't have to take it.

442
00:22:10,120 --> 00:22:16,840
Thank you for being our monitors, your fee will be transferred to your account.
Alright, everyone, let's go home. Yes.

443
00:22:18,080 --> 00:22:23,740
Wait a moment, that was just a joke!
You're being way too cold, Ichinen.

